# Development Rules

## Scope discipline

- One explicit goal per task; honor the non-goal list.
- Do not implement features unless the current task asks for them.
- Keep dependencies minimal — no framework/DB/search/AI SDK until scoped.
- Document limits in `docs/` when closing a phase.

## Commits

- One focused commit per task.
- Conventional Commits (`feat(scope):`, `chore(scope):`, `docs(scope):`).
- Never commit before required validators pass.

## Layout

Respect the repository skeleton:

- `app/knowledge/*` — application modules
- `docs/` — architecture and guides
- `tests/` — future formal suites
- `scripts/` — validation/ops runners
- `docker/` — infra and image scaffolding
- `.cursor/rules/` — persistent agent rules
- `.agents/skills/` — project agent skills
